# "What makes this jurisdiction distinctive" notes for /legal-clinic/what-works/ (Pranoto, 2026-11-13).
# Written with AI assistance from the decisions in the Court Decisions collection and from materials Pranoto supplied:
#   Iskandar 2018 (Social & Legal Studies 27(2), ASEAN), Lyon & Iskandar 2024 (LPCSA 56(3)), Oishi & Chien 2026 (JEMS, East Asia),
#   Farnsworth, The Tools of Argument (reasoning tools), ILO FAIRWAY Gulf factsheets 2023-24. All notes are status "being checked".
# Each entry: key, EN name, ID name, country codes, EN note, ID note, list of (EN, ID) sources beyond the decisions themselves.
J = [
 ('za', 'South Africa', 'Afrika Selatan', ['ZA'],
  'Most rights in the Bill of Rights belong to "everyone", and the Constitutional Court has read that word to include people without South African citizenship. Equality arguments therefore succeed often: permanent residents could not be barred from teaching posts or from social grants. Labour courts have held that a worker without a valid permit is still an employee. Asylum seekers have won a right to work. Public interest organisations bring many of these cases, and the Court can order structural remedies. The limits appear where a job is tied to state security or to the legal profession, where citizenship requirements have been upheld.',
  'Sebagian besar hak dalam Bill of Rights dimiliki "setiap orang", dan Mahkamah Konstitusi membaca kata itu mencakup orang yang bukan warga negara Afrika Selatan. Karena itu argumen kesetaraan sering berhasil: penduduk tetap tidak boleh dihalangi menjadi guru atau menerima bantuan sosial. Pengadilan perburuhan memutuskan bahwa pekerja tanpa izin yang sah tetap seorang pekerja. Pencari suaka memperoleh hak untuk bekerja. Banyak perkara ini diajukan organisasi kepentingan publik, dan Mahkamah bisa memerintahkan pemulihan struktural. Batasnya terlihat pada pekerjaan yang terkait keamanan atau profesi hukum, di mana syarat kewarganegaraan dipertahankan.',
  []),
 ('hk', 'Hong Kong', 'Hong Kong', ['HK'],
  'Hong Kong combines the common law with the Basic Law and a Bill of Rights, but the Bill of Rights Ordinance carries a reservation for immigration matters, and the courts give the government wide room on who may stay. Arguments that foreign domestic helpers should be treated like other residents, for permanent residence or against the live-in rule, have failed. What works better is the criminal law against abusive employers, review of detention, and the torture-screening procedure before removal. Welfare rules that excluded new residents have been struck down where they were disproportionate.',
  'Hong Kong memadukan common law dengan Basic Law dan Bill of Rights, tetapi Bill of Rights Ordinance memuat reservasi untuk urusan imigrasi, dan pengadilan memberi pemerintah keleluasaan luas tentang siapa yang boleh tinggal. Argumen agar pekerja rumah tangga asing diperlakukan seperti penduduk lain, untuk izin tinggal tetap atau melawan kewajiban tinggal di rumah majikan, gagal. Yang lebih berhasil adalah hukum pidana terhadap majikan yang kejam, peninjauan penahanan, dan prosedur penyaringan risiko penyiksaan sebelum pemulangan. Aturan bantuan sosial yang mengecualikan penduduk baru dibatalkan bila tidak proporsional.',
  []),
 ('in', 'India', 'India', ['IN'],
  'The Supreme Court reads the right to life in Article 21 broadly and applies it to every person, citizen or not. Public interest litigation lets organisations, and even a letter, start a case on behalf of bonded or migrant labourers. The Court then issues detailed directions and keeps supervising them, as in the bonded labour cases and the 2021 orders on rations and registration for migrant workers. Foreigners, however, have no constitutional right to reside, so challenges to deportation have usually failed.',
  'Mahkamah Agung membaca hak atas hidup dalam Pasal 21 secara luas dan menerapkannya pada setiap orang, warga negara atau bukan. Litigasi kepentingan publik memungkinkan organisasi, bahkan sepucuk surat, memulai perkara atas nama buruh ijon atau buruh migran. Mahkamah lalu mengeluarkan perintah rinci dan terus mengawasinya, seperti dalam perkara kerja ijon dan perintah tahun 2021 tentang jatah pangan dan pendaftaran buruh migran. Namun orang asing tidak memiliki hak konstitusional untuk menetap, sehingga gugatan terhadap deportasi umumnya gagal.',
  []),
 ('ph', 'Philippines', 'Filipina', ['PH'],
  'The Philippines is a country of origin whose courts discipline the recruitment industry. The Constitution promises full protection to labour at home and overseas, and the Migrant Workers Act makes the local agency liable jointly and severally with the employer abroad. The Supreme Court applies that rule consistently, and it struck down, twice, a cap on the money owed to workers dismissed without cause. Bans on women\'s deployment have been upheld as an exercise of police power, so equality arguments against exit restrictions have not worked here.',
  'Filipina adalah negara asal yang pengadilannya mendisiplinkan industri penempatan. Konstitusi menjanjikan perlindungan penuh bagi pekerja di dalam dan luar negeri, dan Undang-Undang Pekerja Migran membuat agen lokal bertanggung jawab tanggung renteng dengan majikan di luar negeri. Mahkamah Agung menerapkan aturan itu secara konsisten, dan dua kali membatalkan batas uang yang wajib dibayar kepada pekerja yang diberhentikan tanpa alasan. Larangan penempatan perempuan dipertahankan sebagai wewenang negara, sehingga argumen kesetaraan melawan pembatasan keberangkatan tidak berhasil di sini.',
  []),
 ('ca', 'Canada', 'Kanada', ['CA'],
  'The Charter protects "everyone" in its core guarantees, and the Supreme Court treats non-citizenship as a ground of discrimination. Refugee claimants won a right to a fair hearing, and the exclusion of farmworkers from collective bargaining was struck down, although a later, weaker scheme was upheld. Much of the success comes through administrative law, where officers must weigh the best interests of children in humanitarian decisions. When domestic courts refused health care to an irregular migrant, the UN Human Rights Committee later found a violation.',
  'Charter melindungi "setiap orang" dalam jaminan pokoknya, dan Mahkamah Agung memperlakukan status bukan warga negara sebagai dasar diskriminasi. Pemohon status pengungsi memperoleh hak atas pemeriksaan yang adil, dan pengecualian buruh tani dari perundingan kolektif dibatalkan, meski skema pengganti yang lebih lemah kemudian dipertahankan. Banyak keberhasilan datang lewat hukum administrasi, di mana pejabat wajib menimbang kepentingan terbaik anak dalam keputusan kemanusiaan. Ketika pengadilan dalam negeri menolak layanan kesehatan bagi migran tak berdokumen, Komite HAM PBB kemudian menyatakan ada pelanggaran.',
  []),
 ('il', 'Israel', 'Israel', ['IL'],
  'Organisations such as Kav LaOved can petition the Supreme Court directly, sitting as the High Court of Justice, and the Court tests laws for proportionality under the Basic Law on human dignity and liberty. It ended the binding of caregivers to a single employer and struck down a deposit law that withheld wages. It also struck down successive versions of a detention law for asylum seekers, after the Knesset re-enacted them. Arguments on working hours for live-in caregivers and on family reunification have failed.',
  'Organisasi seperti Kav LaOved bisa langsung mengajukan petisi ke Mahkamah Agung yang bersidang sebagai High Court of Justice, dan Mahkamah menguji undang-undang dengan asas proporsionalitas berdasarkan Basic Law tentang martabat dan kebebasan manusia. Mahkamah mengakhiri pengikatan perawat pada satu majikan dan membatalkan undang-undang deposit yang menahan upah. Mahkamah juga membatalkan beberapa versi undang-undang penahanan pencari suaka setelah Knesset memberlakukannya kembali. Argumen tentang jam kerja perawat yang tinggal di rumah majikan dan tentang penyatuan keluarga gagal.',
  []),
 ('jp', 'Japan', 'Jepang', ['JP'],
  'Since the McLean judgment of 1978, Japanese courts have accepted that constitutional rights reach foreigners, but only within the residence system that the Minister of Justice controls with wide discretion. Constitutional challenges on voting, public posts and public assistance have therefore failed. Workers do better in private and criminal law: a worker without a visa recovered lost earnings after an injury, and a technical intern was acquitted. Oishi and Chien (2026) describe Japan\'s welfare system as tied mainly to legal residence status, which matches the pattern in these decisions.',
  'Sejak putusan McLean tahun 1978, pengadilan Jepang menerima bahwa hak konstitusional menjangkau orang asing, tetapi hanya dalam kerangka sistem izin tinggal yang dikendalikan Menteri Kehakiman dengan diskresi luas. Karena itu gugatan konstitusional tentang hak pilih, jabatan publik, dan bantuan sosial gagal. Pekerja lebih berhasil di hukum perdata dan pidana: pekerja tanpa visa memperoleh ganti rugi penghasilan yang hilang setelah cedera, dan seorang pemagang teknis dibebaskan. Oishi dan Chien (2026) menggambarkan sistem kesejahteraan Jepang yang terutama terikat pada status izin tinggal, sejalan dengan pola putusan ini.',
  [('Oishi, N. & Chien, Y.-C. (2026), Migration and transnational health protection in East Asia, Journal of Ethnic and Migration Studies.', 'Oishi, N. & Chien, Y.-C. (2026), Migration and transnational health protection in East Asia, Journal of Ethnic and Migration Studies.')]),
 ('kr', 'South Korea', 'Korea Selatan', ['KR'],
  'Korean courts separate the rights a migrant has as a worker from the structure of the Employment Permit System. Arguments that labour law applies whatever a worker\'s status succeed: trainees are covered by the Labour Standards Act, undocumented workers may form a union, and injured workers without papers receive compensation. Challenges to the limits on changing workplace have failed twice, because the Constitutional Court defers to labour market policy. The Court did strike down indefinite immigration detention in 2023. Oishi and Chien (2026) note that Korea links welfare to residence, employment and family ties.',
  'Pengadilan Korea memisahkan hak migran sebagai pekerja dari struktur Employment Permit System. Argumen bahwa hukum perburuhan berlaku apa pun status pekerja berhasil: peserta pelatihan dilindungi Labour Standards Act, pekerja tak berdokumen boleh membentuk serikat, dan pekerja tanpa dokumen yang cedera menerima kompensasi. Gugatan terhadap pembatasan pindah tempat kerja gagal dua kali, karena Mahkamah Konstitusi menyerahkan kebijakan pasar kerja kepada pemerintah. Mahkamah membatalkan penahanan imigrasi tanpa batas waktu pada 2023. Oishi dan Chien (2026) mencatat bahwa Korea mengaitkan kesejahteraan dengan tempat tinggal, pekerjaan, dan ikatan keluarga.',
  [('Oishi, N. & Chien, Y.-C. (2026), Migration and transnational health protection in East Asia, Journal of Ethnic and Migration Studies.', 'Oishi, N. & Chien, Y.-C. (2026), Migration and transnational health protection in East Asia, Journal of Ethnic and Migration Studies.')]),
 ('tw', 'Taiwan', 'Taiwan', ['TW'],
  'Taiwan\'s Constitutional Court protects personal liberty with firm procedural rules. Detention pending deportation must come quickly before a court, and these arguments have succeeded. Equality claims about benefits and about people from mainland China have failed, because the Court accepts distinctions based on nationality and on cross-strait relations. Taiwan is not a member of the UN or the ILO, so arguments from treaties come through the 2009 act that made the two human rights covenants domestic law.',
  'Mahkamah Konstitusi Taiwan melindungi kebebasan pribadi dengan aturan prosedur yang tegas. Penahanan menunggu deportasi harus segera dibawa ke pengadilan, dan argumen ini berhasil. Gugatan kesetaraan tentang tunjangan dan tentang orang dari Tiongkok daratan gagal, karena Mahkamah menerima pembedaan berdasarkan kewarganegaraan dan hubungan lintas selat. Taiwan bukan anggota PBB atau ILO, sehingga argumen dari perjanjian internasional masuk lewat undang-undang 2009 yang menjadikan dua kovenan HAM sebagai hukum nasional.',
  [('Oishi, N. & Chien, Y.-C. (2026), Migration and transnational health protection in East Asia, Journal of Ethnic and Migration Studies.', 'Oishi, N. & Chien, Y.-C. (2026), Migration and transnational health protection in East Asia, Journal of Ethnic and Migration Studies.')]),
 ('gb', 'United Kingdom', 'Inggris Raya', ['GB'],
  'British cases turn on common law doctrines read together with the European Convention on Human Rights. The Supreme Court held that the illegality defence does not bar a trafficked worker\'s claim, and that neither state immunity nor diplomatic immunity shields an employer from a domestic worker\'s claims. The European Court of Human Rights found that the UK must criminalise and investigate servitude and must not punish victims of trafficking. An argument that discrimination based on immigration status is race discrimination failed.',
  'Perkara di Inggris bertumpu pada doktrin common law yang dibaca bersama Konvensi Eropa tentang HAM. Mahkamah Agung memutuskan bahwa pembelaan "perbuatan melawan hukum" tidak menghalangi gugatan pekerja korban perdagangan orang, dan bahwa kekebalan negara maupun kekebalan diplomatik tidak melindungi majikan dari gugatan pekerja rumah tangga. Pengadilan HAM Eropa menyatakan Inggris wajib memidanakan dan menyelidiki perhambaan serta tidak menghukum korban perdagangan orang. Argumen bahwa diskriminasi karena status imigrasi adalah diskriminasi ras gagal.',
  []),
 ('us', 'United States', 'Amerika Serikat', ['US'],
  'In the United States, Congress has broad power over immigration, but state laws that single out non-citizens face strict review under the equal protection clause. Children without papers won access to public schools, and indefinite detention after a removal order was limited. In the workplace the Supreme Court denied back pay to an undocumented worker under labour law. Workers then took that question to the ILO Committee on Freedom of Association and the Inter-American Commission, which both found against the United States. This shows how an international forum can carry an argument that has failed at home.',
  'Di Amerika Serikat, Kongres memiliki wewenang luas atas imigrasi, tetapi undang-undang negara bagian yang membedakan orang yang bukan warga negara diuji ketat berdasarkan klausul perlindungan setara. Anak tanpa dokumen memperoleh akses ke sekolah negeri, dan penahanan tanpa batas setelah perintah pemulangan dibatasi. Di tempat kerja, Mahkamah Agung menolak upah tertunggak bagi pekerja tak berdokumen berdasarkan hukum perburuhan. Para pekerja lalu membawa soal itu ke Komite Kebebasan Berserikat ILO dan Komisi HAM Antar-Amerika, yang keduanya menyatakan Amerika Serikat bersalah. Ini menunjukkan bagaimana forum internasional bisa meneruskan argumen yang gagal di dalam negeri.',
  []),
 ('sea', 'Southeast Asia (Malaysia, Singapore, Thailand, Indonesia)', 'Asia Tenggara (Malaysia, Singapura, Thailand, Indonesia)', ['MY', 'SG', 'TH', 'ID'],
  'Few constitutional rulings on migrant workers exist in this region. Most decisions in the collection come from criminal courts, where employers who abused domestic workers were convicted in Malaysia and Singapore, though not in every case. They also come from labour and administrative courts, such as Thailand\'s order to compensate Myanmar workers and a Malaysian award against a recruiter. Defamation law has been used against advocates who expose abuse. Iskandar (2018) traces the weakness of rights-based arguments to the region\'s sharp line between legal and illegal foreigners and to the consensus style of ASEAN. He points to national human rights institutions such as SUHAKAM as a home-grown route. In Indonesia, the Constitutional Court kept fishers and ship crew inside the migrant worker protection law. Lyon and Iskandar (2024) show that workers reach the law mainly through trusted intermediaries.',
  'Di kawasan ini hanya ada sedikit putusan konstitusional tentang pekerja migran. Sebagian besar putusan dalam koleksi berasal dari pengadilan pidana, tempat majikan yang menganiaya pekerja rumah tangga dihukum di Malaysia dan Singapura, meski tidak dalam setiap kasus. Putusan lain berasal dari pengadilan perburuhan dan tata usaha negara, seperti perintah Thailand untuk membayar kompensasi kepada pekerja Myanmar dan putusan Malaysia terhadap agen perekrut. Hukum pencemaran nama baik pernah dipakai terhadap pembela yang membongkar pelanggaran. Iskandar (2018) menelusuri lemahnya argumen berbasis hak pada garis tajam antara orang asing legal dan ilegal di kawasan ini serta pada gaya musyawarah ASEAN. Ia menunjuk lembaga HAM nasional seperti SUHAKAM sebagai jalur yang tumbuh dari dalam. Di Indonesia, Mahkamah Konstitusi mempertahankan awak kapal dan nelayan dalam UU pelindungan pekerja migran. Lyon dan Iskandar (2024) menunjukkan bahwa pekerja menjangkau hukum terutama lewat perantara yang mereka percaya.',
  [('Iskandar, P. (2018), Non-Citizen Rights in ASEAN: The Need to Chart a New Course, Social & Legal Studies 27(2): 180–199.', 'Iskandar, P. (2018), Non-Citizen Rights in ASEAN: The Need to Chart a New Course, Social & Legal Studies 27(2): 180–199.'),
   ('Lyon, B. & Iskandar, P. (2024), Relational self and farmworker law reform: the case of Indonesia, Legal Pluralism and Critical Social Analysis 56(3): 616–636.', 'Lyon, B. & Iskandar, P. (2024), Relational self and farmworker law reform: the case of Indonesia, Legal Pluralism and Critical Social Analysis 56(3): 616–636.')]),
 ('gulf', 'Gulf States', 'Negara Teluk', ['AE', 'SA', 'KW', 'QA'],
  'The decisions in the collection from the Gulf States are mostly wage and contract claims in labour courts and courts of cassation. Workers often won these claims, usually on the written terms of the contract and on payment records. A claim normally begins with a complaint to the labour ministry, which tries to settle it before referring it to court. In Kuwait, the Constitutional Court upheld the Domestic Workers Law when recruitment offices challenged it. Practical points for these courts are good documentation and early use of the ministry procedure.',
  'Putusan dari Negara Teluk dalam koleksi ini sebagian besar adalah gugatan upah dan kontrak di pengadilan perburuhan dan pengadilan kasasi. Pekerja sering memenangkan gugatan ini, biasanya berdasarkan isi kontrak tertulis dan catatan pembayaran. Gugatan biasanya dimulai dengan pengaduan ke kementerian ketenagakerjaan, yang berupaya mendamaikan sebelum meneruskannya ke pengadilan. Di Kuwait, Mahkamah Konstitusi mempertahankan Undang-Undang Pekerja Rumah Tangga ketika digugat kantor-kantor perekrutan. Hal praktis di pengadilan ini adalah dokumentasi yang baik dan penggunaan prosedur kementerian sejak awal.',
  [('ILO FAIRWAY, Regulatory framework governing migrant workers: country factsheets for the Gulf States (2023–2024).', 'ILO FAIRWAY, Regulatory framework governing migrant workers: lembar fakta negara-negara Teluk (2023–2024).')]),
]
